Package: rattlerthis
Title: Run Any CLI Tool on a 'Conda' Environment Powered by 'rattler'
Version: 0.0.0.9001
Authors@R:
    person("Lucio", "Queiroz", , "luciorqueiroz@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Creates and manages 'Conda' environments and runs command
    line tools inside them, without shelling out to an external package
    manager binary. Environment solving, package installation, and shell
    activation are implemented natively via Rust bindings (using
    'rextendr') to the 'rattler' library
    (<https://github.com/conda/rattler>), the same engine that powers
    'pixi'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/luciorq/rattlerthis
BugReports: https://github.com/luciorq/rattlerthis/issues
Depends:
    R (>= 4.2)
Imports:
    cli,
    fs,
    jsonlite,
    processx,
    rlang,
    tibble,
    tools,
    withr
Suggests:
    curl,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/Needs/dev: devtools, pkgload, remotes, rcmdcheck, covr, testthat,
    usethis, pak, knitr, quarto, pkgdown, roxygen2, roxygen2md, lintr,
    styler, rextendr
Config/rextendr/version: 0.5.0
Config/roxygen2/markdown: TRUE
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Encoding: UTF-8
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.75.0, OpenSSL on Linux (libssl-dev / openssl-devel)
